## The Strategic Pitch to Heritage Labels (e.g., Blue Note Records)

> "To the modern ear joking that 'nobody plays CDs anymore,' the data offers a different reality: ownership is a luxury good."

If we apply this data-driven framework to an archival vault like Blue Note's legendary catalog, the operational directive changes:

1. Stop treating the catalog as flat digital inventory: Do not rely solely on low-cost MP3 distribution to monetize historic master tapes.
2. Architect tiered monetization: Reserve digital pure-plays for casual discovery, but build limited-edition, multi-format physical/digital bundles for core heritage assets.
3. Monetize the Gen-X / Collector Ethos: Acknowledge that the core demographic keeping legacy genres alive values physical artifacts, premium pressing quality, and archival ownership. Build products for the buyer who is willing to hunt across oceans for a rare import.

